        "original_id": "6b603593-9014-5a5c-aa60-c5a80f0f3627",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ottokar Kernstock, Joseph Haydn\n- Products: \"Sei gesegnet ohne Ende\", \"Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser\", \"Deutschlandlied\"\n- Topics: national anthem of Germany, Classical period, chamber music, piano trio, symphony, string quartet\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph Haydn was born on 31 March 1732 and died on 31 May 1809.\n- Joseph Haydn was an Austrian composer of the Classical period.\n- Joseph Haydn was instrumental in the development of chamber music such as the piano trio.\n- Joseph Haydn's contributions to musical form earned him the epithets \"Father of the Symphony\" and \"Father of the String Quartet\".\n- \"Sei gesegnet ohne Ende\" was written by Ottokar Kernstock.\n- \"Sei gesegnet ohne Ende\" was sung to Joseph Haydn's tune \"Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser\".\n- Joseph Haydn's tune \"Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser\" is also used for the \"Deutschlandlied\".\n- Since 1922, the \"Deutschlandlied\" has been the national anthem of Germany.",
